  "articleBody": "It's tempting to tackle a bathroom floor tile project yourself, and for some super simple, small areas, it might be doable. But for most bathroom floor tiling, especially if you want it to last and look great, bringing in a professional is a really smart move. Why? Well, it goes beyond just laying tiles straight. A pro knows how to properly assess your subfloor for flatness and structural integrity. This is huge! If your floor isn't solid, your tiles won't last. They also understand the importance of movement joints, which prevent cracking due to expansion and contraction, and can skillfully handle transitions to other flooring types. You're also paying for their knowledge of the TCNA (Tile Council of North America) method, which ensures a durable, high-quality installation. If your floor has any deflection issues, existing damage, or if you suspect old lead or asbestos (which is common in older homes), a qualified professional can handle these challenges safely and effectively. Plus, when you're dealing with heavier materials like natural stone, you really need someone experienced to manage the weight and installation. For peace of mind and a job done right, getting help from folks like HH Remodeling LLC is often the best investment, ensuring your new bathroom floor stands the test of time.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}